# axonal_delay_test_neuron.nestml
# ###############################
#
#
# Description
# +++++++++++
#
# Neuron model to test axonal delays. The neuron emits a spike for every spike received on the ``drive_spikes`` port, like a parrot neuron. Spikes received on the other ports are not repeated; instead, the weights of the spikes received in each timestep are recorded in the state variables ``w_received`` (for the generic port ``plastic_spikes``) and ``w_received_lti`` (for the port ``plastic_spikes_lti``, which is intended to be treated as a linear time-invariant port).
#
#
# Copyright statement
# +++++++++++++++++++
